<%# A file page's "Open in <tool>" buttons (Tools::HomeController#open_with), for the lazy frame
    files/show.html.erb points at this. The registry is read HERE, on demand, never by the file
    page. One `.btn` per available tool whose `opens` names the file's extension; a miss of any kind
    renders the frame EMPTY — it sits in the page's actions row, so there is nothing to say.

    `target="_top"` because a link inside a frame otherwise navigates the FRAME, and the tool page
    has no `open-with` frame to answer with (Turbo would log "response has no matching frame" and
    leave the page where it was). The page's own frame carries the same target; both, so the answer
    is right whichever element Turbo consults. %>
<turbo-frame id="open-with" target="_top">
  <% @addons.each do |addon| %>
    <%= link_to "Open in #{addon.title}", tools_addon_path(addon.key, file: @file.node_id), class: "btn" %>
  <% end %>
</turbo-frame>
